[2.1893, "o", "search  weapons and boat furniture. Often he would be surrounded by an eager circle, all waiting\r\n  research  to be served; holding boat-spades, pike-heads, harpoons, and lances, and jealously watch\r\n  research ing his every sooty movement, as he toiled. Nevertheless, this old man's was a patient ha\r\n  research mmer wielded by a patient arm. No murmur, no impatience, no petulance did come from him. \r\n  research Silent, slow, and solemn; bowing over still further his chronically broken back, he toile\r\n  research d away, as if toil were life itself, and the heavy beating of his hammer the heavy beatin\r\n  research g of his heart. And so it was.\u2014Most miserable! A peculiar walk in this old man, a certain\r\n  research  slight but painful appearing yawing in his gait, had at an early period of the voyage ex\r\n  research cited the curiosity of the mariners. And to the importunity of their persisted questionin\r\n  research gs he had finally given in; and so it came to pass that every one now knew the shameful s\r\n  rese"]
[2.1893, "o", "arch tory of his wretched fate. Belated, and not innocently, one bitter winter's midnight, on \r\n  research the road running between two country towns, the blacksmith half-stupidly felt the deadly \r\n  research numbness stealing over him, and sought refuge in a leaning, dilapidated barn. The issue w\r\n  research as, the loss of the extremities of both feet. Out of this revelation, part by part, at la\r\n  research st came out the four acts of the gladness, and the one long, and as yet uncatastrophied f\r\n  research ifth act of the grief of his life's drama. He was an old man, who, at the age of nearly s\r\n  research ixty, had p\",\"kind\":\"document\",\"id\":\"e9ee32f7-3909-4b0c-8811-24bdb9f7a974:p2\",\"snapshotId\r\n  research \":\"e9ee32f7-3909-4b0c-8811-24bdb9f7a974\",\"url\":\"https://httpbin.org/html\"}]}\r\n"]
